{"name":"Jakarta","hex":"#efddc3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Jakarta","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A province and capital city of Indonesia.","The Indonesian government."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Jakarta"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jakarta","blocks":[{"text":"Jakarta, officially the Special Capital Region of Jakarta, is the capital and largest city of Indonesia, with administrative status equivalent to a province. It lies on the northwestern coast of Java, bordering West Java and Banten and facing the Java Sea. Jakarta covers about 662 square kilometres and had 11 million registered residents in 2025. Its urban area extends well beyond the provincial boundary into the wider Jakarta metropolitan area, which had a population of nearly 42 million in 2025 according to the United Nations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Bundaran_Hotel_Indonesia_%282025%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Bundaran_Hotel_Indonesia_%282025%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jakarta","wikidata":"Q3630"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Thamrin_dari_Hotel_Take%27s_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Thamrin_dari_Hotel_Take%27s_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Thamrin_dari_Hotel_Take%27s_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Thamrin_dari_Hotel_Take%27s_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Thamrin_dari_Hotel_Take%27s_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Thamrin_dari_Hotel_Take%27s_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThamrin_dari_Hotel_Take's_(cropped).jpg"},{"s